  "title": "On genuine two-dimensional space only parity reproduces itself with a knot",
  "subject": "Which three-bit knot rules on the triangular lattice are exact under subdivision with shared boundaries, and what their solutions keep of emergence",
  "conclusion": "On the triangular lattice with shared subdivision, only 22 of 122 knot rules reproduce themselves exactly at scale 2 and 6 at scale 3, all with affine solution sets and zero entropy density: parity (Newman-Moore, Baxter-Wu), rules equal to parity on tori, and twisted not-all-equal collapsed to equality lines. Exactness on genuine two-dimensional space keeps a knot only through parity; not-all-equal never reproduces itself.",
